{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Blessed be He who enlarges Gad.</b> Because the inheritance of Gad was in a place of pasture, as it is said: ״ומקנה רב היה לבני גד״ etc., it is fitting to use the language of enlargement regarding him, as it is written: ״ורעו במרחב״." "<b>And he tore the arm, even the scalp.</b> The Rav explained בכור שור: for when he would strike, and the one struck would raise his arm so that he not be hit on the head, he would sever the arm along with the head, and drive the blow deep until the end of the shoulder."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:03.524512905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}